# Line endings are fixed per file type, never left to core.autocrlf. A formatting
# gate that reads different bytes on a Windows checkout than on a Linux runner is
# not a gate: it either fails for a reason the author cannot reproduce or, worse,
# passes locally and fails in CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.pro text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf

# gradlew and gradlew.bat are left alone on purpose: the shell script and the
# batch file each need their own ending in the worktree, and their committed
# blobs already carry it.

# Binary assets must never be touched by an end-of-line conversion.
*.apk binary
*.aar binary
*.so binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.jar binary